    <briefdescription>
<para>A sequential neural network composed of an ordered collection of layers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network" kindref="compound">Network</ref> class represents a feedforward neural network in which an input tensor is passed sequentially through each layer in the order they were added. The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network" kindref="compound">Network</ref> holds raw pointers to its <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Layer" kindref="compound">Layer</ref> objects as well as shared pointers to all learnable parameter tensors across the network. <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network" kindref="compound">Network</ref> objects are intended to be constructed via the <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1NetworkBuilder" kindref="compound">NetworkBuilder</ref> class, which provides a fluent interface for assembling layers and collecting their parameters.</para>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network" kindref="compound">Network</ref> class also provides functionality for saving and loading the learned parameter values to and from CSV files, as well as generating a text summary of the network architecture.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1NetworkBuilder" kindref="compound">NetworkBuilder</ref> for the builder class used to construct <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network" kindref="compound">Network</ref> objects. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Layer" kindref="compound">Layer</ref> for the base class from which all network <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network_1a4691637c25d1e76572e5c813b9bad690" kindref="member">layers</ref> derive. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Optimiser" kindref="compound">Optimiser</ref> for the classes that optimise the <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Network_1a42f469fa5c54970d501e23de76f2298c" kindref="member">parameters</ref> of this network. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
